<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="2.639" dur="3">USA.</text><text start="16.32" dur="4.4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you. Thank you. And God bless each</text><text start="18.88" dur="5.8">and every one of you. And God bless the</text><text start="20.72" dur="3.96">United States of America.</text><text start="29.359" dur="3.24">I see.</text><text start="34.64" dur="7.919">I see trouble on the way.</text><text start="40" dur="5.559">I see</text><text start="42.559" dur="3">lightning.</text><text start="53.12" dur="7.56">Please welcome the Speaker of the</text><text start="55.76" dur="4.92">Michigan House, Matt Hall.</text><text start="67.119" dur="8.201">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; First things first, I&amp;#39;m</text><text start="70.88" dur="4.44">headd up.</text><text start="78.64" dur="5.2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; All right. Well, great. Well, I&amp;#39;m</text><text start="81.52" dur="6.919">excited to be here today with President</text><text start="83.84" dur="4.599">Donald J. Trump. What about you?</text><text start="90.88" dur="4.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Now, I&amp;#39;ve worked closely with President</text><text start="92.88" dur="5.199">Trump on Michigan&amp;#39;s biggest issues, and</text><text start="95.6" dur="5.6">I&amp;#39;ve seen firsthand how hard he fights</text><text start="98.079" dur="6.161">for our state. President Trump has done</text><text start="101.2" dur="5.76">something politicians have talked about</text><text start="104.24" dur="4.879">for decades, but never delivered, and</text><text start="106.96" dur="5.04">that is lowering our prescription drug</text><text start="109.119" dur="5.881">prices. the biggest drop in more than 60</text><text start="112" dur="3">years.</text><text start="118.159" dur="5.28">President Trump forced drug companies to</text><text start="120.479" dur="6">give Americans the same low prices they</text><text start="123.439" dur="5.52">give other countries. Trump RX has</text><text start="126.479" dur="7.12">already saved families almost a billion</text><text start="128.959" dur="8.041">dollars with some drugs cut 50%, 70% or</text><text start="133.599" dur="3.401">even 90%.</text><text start="140.8" dur="6">Now, every Medicaid program, every state</text><text start="143.92" dur="6.959">Medicaid program in America is getting</text><text start="146.8" dur="7.519">those lower prices nearly $65 billion</text><text start="150.879" dur="6.161">over the next decade. And I can tell you</text><text start="154.319" dur="6.401">even our Democrat governor signed up for</text><text start="157.04" dur="5.6">it for our state medicaid program. It</text><text start="160.72" dur="5.04">was too good of a deal for her to pass</text><text start="162.64" dur="5.679">up. And that&amp;#39;s the art of the deal. Here</text><text start="165.76" dur="4.96">in Michigan, we&amp;#39;re pairing those savings</text><text start="168.319" dur="4.961">with reforms to make Medicaid stronger</text><text start="170.72" dur="5.519">and sustainable. We&amp;#39;re cutting waste,</text><text start="173.28" dur="5.52">fraud, and abuse, kicking fraudsters and</text><text start="176.239" dur="5.961">illegal aliens off of Medicaid, and</text><text start="178.8" dur="3.4">making sure</text><text start="186.879" dur="4.961">and making sure Medicaid is there for</text><text start="189.12" dur="6.08">families who truly need it, not</text><text start="191.84" dur="5.039">able-bodied adults, 40-year-old men</text><text start="195.2" dur="4.48">sitting in their parents&amp;#39; basement</text><text start="196.879" dur="5.961">playing video games while taxpayers foot</text><text start="199.68" dur="3.16">the bill.</text><text start="206.159" dur="5.121">That&amp;#39;s why President Trump brought back</text><text start="208.319" dur="5.521">work requirements. If able-bodied adults</text><text start="211.28" dur="4.879">want taxpayer funded health care, they</text><text start="213.84" dur="4.479">should be working, studying, training,</text><text start="216.159" dur="5.561">or serving their community. That is</text><text start="218.319" dur="3.401">common sense.</text><text start="224.319" dur="5.361">But federal reforms only work if states</text><text start="226.879" dur="5.36">carry them out. That&amp;#39;s why at the state</text><text start="229.68" dur="5.279">level, Michigan House Republicans put</text><text start="232.239" dur="4.72">resources and real accountability into</text><text start="234.959" dur="4.961">state law to implement the work</text><text start="236.959" dur="4.56">requirements, verify eligibility, and</text><text start="239.92" dur="4.72">make them work as President Trump</text><text start="241.519" dur="5.44">intended. We&amp;#39;re also auditing autism</text><text start="244.64" dur="5.04">providers and measuring child care</text><text start="246.959" dur="5.681">attendance so taxpayers pay only for</text><text start="249.68" dur="7.24">real services. Minnesota style fraud</text><text start="252.64" dur="4.28">will not happen here in Michigan.</text><text start="261.44" dur="5.68">President Trump is also investing $50</text><text start="264.32" dur="5.84">billion to strengthen rural hospitals</text><text start="267.12" dur="6.96">and rural healthcare. In Michigan, we</text><text start="270.16" dur="6.08">received $173 million in year one and</text><text start="274.08" dur="4.96">your state house Republicans are making</text><text start="276.24" dur="5.12">sure it supports local hospitals, more</text><text start="279.04" dur="5.12">doctors and nurses, and better care</text><text start="281.36" dur="7.32">closer to home. That is President Trump</text><text start="284.16" dur="4.52">delivering for Michigan. Again,</text><text start="292.24" dur="4.72">President Trump&amp;#39;s great healthc care</text><text start="294.16" dur="5.2">plan puts patients first with more</text><text start="296.96" dur="5.04">transparency and an end to government</text><text start="299.36" dur="4.8">payoffs for big insurance companies. And</text><text start="302" dur="5.039">we&amp;#39;re bringing that same patient first</text><text start="304.16" dur="6.08">approach to lancing. clear prices before</text><text start="307.039" dur="5.761">treatment, ending hidden facility fees,</text><text start="310.24" dur="5.2">and bann banning predatory medical debt</text><text start="312.8" dur="5.04">practices. I&amp;#39;m taking on the hospital</text><text start="315.44" dur="5.36">and insurance lobbies who&amp;#39;ve driven up</text><text start="317.84" dur="7.16">costs higher for years. I don&amp;#39;t work for</text><text start="320.8" dur="4.2">them, I work for you.</text><text start="327.36" dur="4.24">And that&amp;#39;s why President Trump needs</text><text start="329.28" dur="5.12">strong allies in Michigan to keep these</text><text start="331.6" dur="4.72">reforms moving. Now, here locally,</text><text start="334.4" dur="4.639">you&amp;#39;ve got a great state representative</text><text start="336.32" dur="6.04">and Joe Pavlov who&amp;#39;s doing a great job</text><text start="339.039" dur="3.321">for you.</text><text start="342.479" dur="4.241">And I see Jay Deoer here who&amp;#39;s done a</text><text start="344.88" dur="4.84">fantastic job, our next lieutenant</text><text start="346.72" dur="3">governor.</text><text start="349.84" dur="4.799">Uh but also in the state senate, you&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="352.08" dur="5.28">got Andrew Beer, uh who&amp;#39;s a fighter for</text><text start="354.639" dur="5.681">you, and John Goldwater, who&amp;#39;s going to</text><text start="357.36" dur="4.96">flip a Democrat seat red and deliver a</text><text start="360.32" dur="5">Senate Republican majority here in</text><text start="362.32" dur="3">Michigan.</text><text start="367.44" dur="5.36">With Republican majorities, we can pass</text><text start="370.16" dur="6">my plan to eliminate the state property</text><text start="372.8" dur="6.6">tax, saving the average homeowner $1,000</text><text start="376.16" dur="3.24">a year.</text><text start="381.28" dur="4.88">We can repeal Democrat green energy</text><text start="383.68" dur="4.639">mandates and force utilities to roll</text><text start="386.16" dur="4.24">back their rates a billion dollars,</text><text start="388.319" dur="5.081">wiping out the last three years of rate</text><text start="390.4" dur="3">increases.</text><text start="394" dur="4.639">And we can break the grip of the health</text><text start="396.08" dur="5.44">care lobbyists and dramatically lower</text><text start="398.639" dur="5.12">health care costs for Michigan families.</text><text start="401.52" dur="4.959">Now, President Trump has delivered for</text><text start="403.759" dur="5.28">us time and time again. We&amp;#39;ve seen it at</text><text start="406.479" dur="4.801">Selfridge Air National Guard Base. We&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="409.039" dur="5.841">seen it with the tax cuts, the biggest</text><text start="411.28" dur="5.919">in in history, better trade deals, and</text><text start="414.88" dur="5.439">lower prescription drug costs. But</text><text start="417.199" dur="6">President Trump cannot do this alone. We</text><text start="420.319" dur="5.921">have to do our part. We have to turn out</text><text start="423.199" dur="6.801">in record numbers and vote. Don&amp;#39;t let</text><text start="426.24" dur="6.56">fake polls trick you from the fake news.</text><text start="430" dur="5.199">They are trying to suppress our vote.</text><text start="432.8" dur="5.44">That is what they want. ignore the fake</text><text start="435.199" dur="5.681">polls and get out and vote. We need to</text><text start="438.24" dur="8.12">swamp the vote for Republicans in every</text><text start="440.88" dur="5.48">single race and make it too big to rig.</text><text start="446.88" dur="3.24">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you.</text><text start="460.16" dur="3.479">All the words.</text><text start="476.8" dur="4.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Please welcome the Republican nominee</text><text start="479.36" dur="6.6">for Michigan&amp;#39;s 10th Congressional</text><text start="481.44" dur="4.52">District, Mike Bousard.</text><text start="498.319" dur="3.801">Sun coming up.</text><text start="504.72" dur="4.96">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Holy cow, LOOK AT THIS CROWD. ARE YOU</text><text start="506.639" dur="5.361">GUYS FIRED UP?</text><text start="509.68" dur="5.88">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Are you fired UP TO FIGHT FOR THE FUTURE</text><text start="512" dur="3.56">OF OUR COUNTRY?</text><text start="516.88" dur="3.2">You know, this time last year, I had</text><text start="518.64" dur="3.839">just gotten back from a combat</text><text start="520.08" dur="3.759">deployment to Iraq. And the very next</text><text start="522.479" dur="3.761">day, I started running for this</text><text start="523.839" dur="5.041">congressional seat because the seat I&amp;#39;m</text><text start="526.24" dur="4.56">running for, my district, the Michigan</text><text start="528.88" dur="5.2">10th Congressional District, needs a</text><text start="530.8" dur="6.32">fighter. Our country needs fighters. And</text><text start="534.08" dur="5.52">if we lose this seat, we are likely to</text><text start="537.12" dur="5.48">lose the House to these radical extreme</text><text start="539.6" dur="3">leftists.</text><text start="545.44" dur="5.839">Now, if Hakeem Jeff is in the majority,</text><text start="548.88" dur="4.639">he will listen and bow to whatever</text><text start="551.279" dur="5.12">demands the Democrat socialists throw at</text><text start="553.519" dur="7.88">him. And my opponent, Christina Hines,</text><text start="556.399" dur="5">would be a liberal rubber stamp vote.</text><text start="565.44" dur="3.36">You know, some Democrats might pretend</text><text start="567.12" dur="3.92">to be moderates, but they will always</text><text start="568.8" dur="4.8">vote in lock step with their party&amp;#39;s</text><text start="571.04" dur="4.96">agenda. If there&amp;#39;s a vote to let men</text><text start="573.6" dur="5.88">into women&amp;#39;s locker rooms, my opponent&amp;#39;s</text><text start="576" dur="3.48">going to vote for it.</text><text start="581.839" dur="3.12">If there&amp;#39;s a vote to impeach the</text><text start="583.279" dur="4.841">president, my opponent&amp;#39;s going to vote</text><text start="584.959" dur="3.161">for it.</text><text start="589.12" dur="3.2">And if there&amp;#39;s a vote to open the</text><text start="590.56" dur="5.16">southern border, my opponent is going to</text><text start="592.32" dur="3.4">vote for it.</text><text start="595.92" dur="3.2">She has already said that she believes</text><text start="597.519" dur="5.201">every single person in this country</text><text start="599.12" dur="6.56">illegally deserves amnesty.</text><text start="602.72" dur="5.84">and amnesty was the sole tenant she</text><text start="605.68" dur="4.96">followed as a prosecutor.</text><text start="608.56" dur="4.16">She let off a human trafficker. She</text><text start="610.64" dur="4.48">dropped all charges when there was a</text><text start="612.72" dur="4.48">mountain of evidence and that man</text><text start="615.12" dur="4.88">continued trafficking and was arrested</text><text start="617.2" dur="5.04">in my district in Warren, Michigan.</text><text start="620" dur="4.079">My opponent also agreed to a plea deal</text><text start="622.24" dur="5.4">and gave a man who raped a 12-year-old</text><text start="624.079" dur="3.561">girl probation.</text><text start="630.72" dur="4.72">And most recently, she has started</text><text start="632.48" dur="5.76">attacking these victims, the victims who</text><text start="635.44" dur="5.92">called her out for letting her down. And</text><text start="638.24" dur="4.88">her response was to attack that victim.</text><text start="641.36" dur="3.76">Even Christina Hines&amp;#39;s own colleagues</text><text start="643.12" dur="4.88">have said, &amp;quot;Shame on her for attacking</text><text start="645.12" dur="4.88">the victims.&amp;quot; We cannot let people like</text><text start="648" dur="4">this set the course of our country&amp;#39;s</text><text start="650" dur="4.48">future.</text><text start="652" dur="4.56">Now, we need to put America first. We</text><text start="654.48" dur="4.32">need policies that will help the</text><text start="656.56" dur="4.959">hardworking families across my district,</text><text start="658.8" dur="5.92">this state, and this country. We cannot</text><text start="661.519" dur="4.641">allow crazy ideology to govern us. My</text><text start="664.72" dur="3.76">opponent said she is thrilled to work</text><text start="666.16" dur="6.239">with the Jane Fonda Climate Pack. Now,</text><text start="668.48" dur="5.28">if you don&amp;#39;t know what that is,</text><text start="672.399" dur="2.88">now if you don&amp;#39;t know what that is,</text><text start="673.76" dur="3.68">here&amp;#39;s here I&amp;#39;ll tell you what it is.</text><text start="675.279" dur="4.721">They are group that wants to ban gas</text><text start="677.44" dur="5.56">powered cars and end the fossil fuel</text><text start="680" dur="3">industry.</text><text start="684.8" dur="4">In the auto capital of the world,</text><text start="687.2" dur="5.28">somebody running to represent this</text><text start="688.8" dur="5.44">district wants to ban gaspowered cars.</text><text start="692.48" dur="4.32">Talk about not representing your</text><text start="694.24" dur="4.24">district. Talk about not representing</text><text start="696.8" dur="3.84">the people that you are saying that you</text><text start="698.48" dur="4">want to run for. We cannot afford these</text><text start="700.64" dur="5.96">terrible policies and we sure as heck</text><text start="702.48" dur="4.12">cannot afford Christina Hines.</text><text start="713.68" dur="5.44">Now, I got back from Iraq on a simple</text><text start="716.399" dur="4.801">mission to lower costs, keep our</text><text start="719.12" dur="7">communities safe, and make sure that our</text><text start="721.2" dur="4.92">jobs and our auto workers stay local.</text><text start="729.68" dur="4.8">I haven&amp;#39;t taken a day off in almost two</text><text start="731.76" dur="6">years because I believe in America.</text><text start="734.48" dur="5.52">But our country, we are at a crossroads.</text><text start="737.76" dur="6.84">If we win in November, we can guarantee</text><text start="740" dur="4.6">another 250 years of freedom.</text><text start="749.68" dur="3.76">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We&amp;#39;re not going to let people who hate</text><text start="751.36" dur="5.68">this country chip away at it block by</text><text start="753.44" dur="5.68">block. And it is on you and I. It is on</text><text start="757.04" dur="4.08">us to make sure that we get to the polls</text><text start="759.12" dur="4.56">on November 3rd. We need to build this</text><text start="761.12" dur="4.719">country up. We need to work every single</text><text start="763.68" dur="4.56">day between now and November 3rd to make</text><text start="765.839" dur="4.481">sure we bring this home. I have seen a</text><text start="768.24" dur="4.08">lot of other countries. I&amp;#39;ve seen other</text><text start="770.32" dur="4.16">forms of government. And I can tell you</text><text start="772.32" dur="3.68">without a doubt in my mind, the United</text><text start="774.48" dur="5.64">States of America is the greatest</text><text start="776" dur="4.12">country there has ever been.</text><text start="788.079" dur="3">USA.</text><text start="797.839" dur="4.56">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; You know, you guys fill me with hope for</text><text start="799.76" dur="4.8">our future and for our country.</text><text start="802.399" dur="4">Somewhere along the way, some believe it</text><text start="804.56" dur="4.88">became controversial to say we love our</text><text start="806.399" dur="4.721">country. But not us. Because you and I</text><text start="809.44" dur="3.199">know that America is still the beacon on</text><text start="811.12" dur="3.6">the hill that the rest of the world</text><text start="812.639" dur="4.88">looks to. The way we keep it like that</text><text start="814.72" dur="5.6">is to vote. I need you to make sure that</text><text start="817.519" dur="5.201">you and everybody you know, whether now</text><text start="820.32" dur="4.4">on early voting, turning in absentee</text><text start="822.72" dur="4.239">ballots, or voting on election day, make</text><text start="824.72" dur="5.96">sure you vote because our future sure as</text><text start="826.959" dur="3.721">heck depends on it.</text><text start="835.839" dur="3.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; God bless you all. God bless Michigan</text><text start="838.079" dur="5.88">and God bless the United States of</text><text start="839.519" dur="4.44">America. Thank you guys so much.</text><text start="869.12" dur="4.399">Please welcome the chairwoman of the</text><text start="871.519" dur="6.361">House Republican Conference,</text><text start="873.519" dur="4.361">Congresswoman Lisa Mlan.</text><text start="910.32" dur="5.639">It is good to be in my district.</text><text start="917.6" dur="6.76">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Hey poor here on MICHIGAN 9TH. ARE YOU</text><text start="920.56" dur="3.8">READY TO WIN THIS THING?</text><text start="924.56" dur="6.24">I will tell you, it is such an honor to</text><text start="927.519" dur="5.201">be home in Michigan&amp;#39;s ninth. Yes, I&amp;#39;m a</text><text start="930.8" dur="5.64">little biased, but the best district</text><text start="932.72" dur="3.72">there is in Congress.</text><text start="937.36" dur="6.32">And I will say humbly, it is my honor to</text><text start="941.6" dur="6.44">represent you all. So, thank you for</text><text start="943.68" dur="4.36">giving me the honor to do that.</text><text start="951.199" dur="7.801">and President Trump,</text><text start="953.759" dur="5.241">thank you for coming to Michigan.</text><text start="961.36" dur="7.839">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Now, when I look around this room, I see</text><text start="964.32" dur="7.879">farmers, auto workers, moms, dads, and</text><text start="969.199" dur="3">veterans.</text><text start="972.32" dur="7.28">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I see the soul of this country right</text><text start="976.079" dur="3.521">here in Michigan.</text><text start="980.8" dur="7.44">And today we are nine days away from an</text><text start="984.8" dur="6.32">election that will decide the future of</text><text start="988.24" dur="6.159">our great state. And I&amp;#39;ll tell you what</text><text start="991.12" dur="7.519">keeps me up at night. It&amp;#39;s the communist</text><text start="994.399" dur="7.841">crazy we&amp;#39;re seeing on the left.</text><text start="998.639" dur="7.12">It is the thought of what happens to our</text><text start="1002.24" dur="6.64">children, our families, and our country</text><text start="1005.759" dur="4.721">if we let the radical left take us</text><text start="1008.88" dur="3.68">backwards.</text><text start="1010.48" dur="5.76">Because this election is a contrast</text><text start="1012.56" dur="7.76">between common sense and communist</text><text start="1016.24" dur="8.68">crazy. And I will share with you, WE ARE</text><text start="1020.32" dur="4.6">THE PARTY OF COMMON SENSE.</text><text start="1025.52" dur="4.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; That&amp;#39;s right.</text><text start="1027.439" dur="5.52">And ladies and gentlemen, commun</text><text start="1030" dur="5.839">communist crazy has a price. Then the</text><text start="1032.959" dur="6.321">people who pay that price aren&amp;#39;t sitting</text><text start="1035.839" dur="6.72">in an office in Washington DC. They are</text><text start="1039.28" dur="6.279">all of you sitting here in this room</text><text start="1042.559" dur="3">tonight.</text><text start="1046.959" dur="5.761">Now think about it for a minute. Think</text><text start="1049.28" dur="7.6">about your paycheck and everything you</text><text start="1052.72" dur="7.839">did to earn it. The alarm clock goes off</text><text start="1056.88" dur="6.32">before dawn. The extra shifts you you</text><text start="1060.559" dur="7.041">work when the furnace quits. Every</text><text start="1063.2" dur="7.44">single dollar in that paycheck is yours.</text><text start="1067.6" dur="5.439">It&amp;#39;s your time, your money, your grit,</text><text start="1070.64" dur="5.279">and your sacrifice.</text><text start="1073.039" dur="6">Now, for one moment, picture that money</text><text start="1075.919" dur="6.321">walking out the door. And why? Because</text><text start="1079.039" dur="6.561">Democrats tax the hell out of it to give</text><text start="1082.24" dur="5.439">it to illegals.</text><text start="1085.6" dur="4.8">I will tell you ladies and gentlemen</text><text start="1087.679" dur="5.281">that is the Democratic agenda. Now I</text><text start="1090.4" dur="4.72">built a business in Michigan and I know</text><text start="1092.96" dur="4.16">that that paycheck</text><text start="1095.12" dur="3.439">what I know what that paycheck means to</text><text start="1097.12" dur="4.799">you. I know what it means to your</text><text start="1098.559" dur="6.401">family. That&amp;#39;s why Republicans fought</text><text start="1101.919" dur="5.12">for you to keep more of it. I know that</text><text start="1104.96" dur="4.32">a paycheck is more than a number on a</text><text start="1107.039" dur="4">piece of paper. It&amp;#39;s dance lessons for</text><text start="1109.28" dur="4.32">your daughter. It&amp;#39;s winter tires for</text><text start="1111.039" dur="5.52">your truck. But I want to remind you,</text><text start="1113.6" dur="7.319">those dollars are your money. That&amp;#39;s</text><text start="1116.559" dur="4.36">your hard-earned tax dollars.</text><text start="1121.44" dur="4.32">And you know what the 