lican you&amp;#39;re talking</text><text start="8733.12" dur="3.199">about, that would be the biggest story</text><text start="8734.56" dur="3.28">in the country. You know that, Mike.</text><text start="8736.319" dur="4.08">That would be the biggest story in the</text><text start="8737.84" dur="5.36">country. In much less than two years, we</text><text start="8740.399" dur="5.04">secured commitments for 22.2 2 trillion</text><text start="8743.2" dur="4.8">dollars of new investment into the</text><text start="8745.439" dur="5.281">United States of America. The greatest</text><text start="8748" dur="5.84">amount of money ever invested in our</text><text start="8750.72" dur="6.16">country by five times. It&amp;#39;s the single</text><text start="8753.84" dur="5.12">greatest investment into a country in</text><text start="8756.88" dur="4.559">history. And that includes China and all</text><text start="8758.96" dur="5.2">the rest I love. And thanks to my</text><text start="8761.439" dur="4.721">tariffs, we have more factories and</text><text start="8764.16" dur="4">plants being built in the United States</text><text start="8766.16" dur="4.08">right now than at any time in the</text><text start="8768.16" dur="5.04">history. And you see it all over your</text><text start="8770.24" dur="2.96">state.</text><text start="8775.04" dur="4">And because of me, the auto industry is</text><text start="8777.12" dur="4.56">doing better than it&amp;#39;s ever done before</text><text start="8779.04" dur="5.52">with plants and factories being built at</text><text start="8781.68" dur="6.16">a record clip and also being expanded</text><text start="8784.56" dur="7.36">all over the country, but especially</text><text start="8787.84" dur="7.68">in Michigan. You know, you have a an old</text><text start="8791.92" dur="5.2">I think it&amp;#39;s a 1901 building, Ford, and</text><text start="8795.52" dur="3.28">uh I saw them, they were going to close</text><text start="8797.12" dur="3.12">it. It&