 of</text><text start="9206" dur="4.8">Michigan.</text><text start="9208.08" dur="5.92">You&amp;#39;re voting for Anthony Forini, my</text><text start="9210.8" dur="6.4">county clerk, who makes sure there&amp;#39;s no</text><text start="9214" dur="6.08">fraud going on on election day.</text><text start="9217.2" dur="5.68">And you&amp;#39;re voting for Doug Lloyd, a guy</text><text start="9220.08" dur="6.279">who prosecutes criminals. He doesn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="9222.88" dur="3.479">protect them.</text><text start="9226.88" dur="4.24">Right.</text><text start="9228.96" dur="4.56">And it&amp;#39;s an honor. I&amp;#39;m sitting over here</text><text start="9231.12" dur="4.64">with these guys and it&amp;#39;s an honor to be</text><text start="9233.52" dur="5.44">associated with them. What a great</text><text start="9235.76" dur="6.639">ticket we have. Up and down the ticket,</text><text start="9238.96" dur="6">every single office, our candidates are</text><text start="9242.399" dur="7.241">10 times better than the whack jobs</text><text start="9244.96" dur="4.68">they&amp;#39;re running on the Democrat side.</text><text start="9250.72" dur="6.16">Now, I&amp;#39;m only going to say one thing</text><text start="9253.2" dur="5.84">about Abdul Akman Muhammad El Say</text><text start="9256.88" dur="3.92">because everybody else has been telling</text><text start="9259.04" dur="4.8">you about him and you guys know about</text><text start="9260.8" dur="5.599">him. But as an auto worker, I&amp;#39;m a</text><text start="9263.84" dur="4.88">retiree now and I&amp;#39;ve got Blue Cross</text><text start="9266.399" dur="5.521">Healthcare. It&amp;#39;s the best in the</text><text start="9268.72" dur="5.679">country. Nobody has better health care.</text><text start="9271.92" dur="5.04">They call it the Cadillac plan. We spent</text><text start="9274.399" dur="5.04">the last five decades negotiating for</text><text start="9276.96" dur="6.56">it. You know what say wants to do with</text><text start="9279.439" dur="6.401">it? Scrap it. Ban it. Make it illegal.</text><text start="9283.52" dur="7.36">Everybody&amp;#39;s got to go on Medicare,</text><text start="9285.84" dur="7.12">governmentrun healthcare. Like Canada.</text><text start="9290.88" dur="4">Now we&amp;#39;re we&amp;#39;re just a couple of miles.</text><text start="9292.96" dur="5.04">You look out. You step outside, look</text><text start="9294.88" dur="5.36">across the river, you see Canada. They</text><text start="9298" dur="5.12">come over here to get emergency</text><text start="9300.24" dur="6.6">procedures done because governmentr run</text><text start="9303.12" dur="3.72">healthc care sucks.</text><text start="9309.92" dur="6.64">Right? We all know this. So, everybody</text><text start="9313.52" dur="4.959">in this building is voting for the</text><text start="9316.56" dur="4.56">gentleman I just mentioned because</text><text start="9318.479" dur="4.88">they&amp;#39;re great candidates. But our job</text><text start="9321.12" dur="5.12">when we leave here, and we&amp;#39;re the</text><text start="9323.359" dur="5.681">soldiers. This guy&amp;#39;s the general. We&amp;#39;re</text><text start="9326.24" dur="6">the soldiers. So to keep his agenda</text><text start="9329.04" dur="5.04">moving forward when we leave here, not</text><text start="9332.24" dur="5.04">only do we all have to make sure that</text><text start="9334.08" dur="6.16">we&amp;#39;ve voted by tomorrow, we&amp;#39;ve got to go</text><text start="9337.28" dur="5.52">through our phone list. You text your</text><text start="9340.24" dur="5.199">family members, your neighbors, your</text><text start="9342.8" dur="5.28">friends, your co-workers, and you work</text><text start="9345.439" dur="5.761">your way through that phone contact list</text><text start="9348.08" dur="5.84">until you&amp;#39;ve texted every single person</text><text start="9351.2" dur="6.64">in there and reminded them that Michigan</text><text start="9353.92" dur="6.96">has early in-person voting. that started</text><text start="9357.84" dur="5.36">yesterday on the 24th and they need to</text><text start="9360.88" dur="4">get their butts out and vote. I don&amp;#39;t</text><text start="9363.2" dur="5.04">care if they&amp;#39;re paying a buck and a half</text><text start="9364.88" dur="7.04">more a gallon for gasoline. That is no</text><text start="9368.24" dur="7.56">excuse to vote for a socialist Islamist</text><text start="9371.92" dur="3.88">for the US Senate.</text><text start="9376.72" dur="4.639">And when you don&amp;#39;t vote, you might as</text><text start="9379.12" dur="4.319">well be voting for a Democrat because</text><text start="9381.359" dur="4">you&amp;#39;re taking a vote away from these</text><text start="9383.439" dur="4.241">excellent candidates sitting right over</text><text start="9385.359" dur="4.561">here.</text><text start="9387.68" dur="4.719">So when we walk out of here, everybody</text><text start="9389.92" dur="4.479">needs to know you got a job to do.</text><text start="9392.399" dur="4.881">You&amp;#39;re all warriors. You&amp;#39;re all patriots</text><text start="9394.399" dur="4.96">or you wouldn&amp;#39;t be here. So get out and</text><text start="9397.28" dur="4">get go through your phone list. Talk to</text><text start="9399.359" dur="4.721">everybody. If you&amp;#39;re going to work</text><text start="9401.28" dur="5.52">tomorrow, talk about politics. Talk</text><text start="9404.08" dur="5.12">about the future of our country. 250</text><text start="9406.8" dur="4.24">years ago, people signed the Declaration</text><text start="9409.2" dur="3.84">of Independence. You know what that was?</text><text start="9411.04" dur="4.48">It was a death sentence. If we didn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="9413.04" dur="5.439">win that war, they were going to hang.</text><text start="9415.52" dur="5.68">We owe it to them to fight for what they</text><text start="9418.479" dur="6.401">fought for back then and preserve it for</text><text start="9421.2" dur="5.44">another 250 years. Thank you, Mr.</text><text start="9424.88" dur="5.16">President. Thank you for everything</text><text start="9426.64" dur="3.4">you&amp;#39;ve done.</text><text start="9441.68" dur="3">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Wow.</text><text start="9445.6" dur="5.12">What a guy he is. Well, now I can get</text><text start="9448.88" dur="3.28">rid of a couple of paragraphs of this.</text><text start="9450.72" dur="4.4">We don&amp;#39;t have to talk about healthcare</text><text start="9452.16" dur="4.8">anymore. He&amp;#39;s right. He&amp;#39;s right. Other</text><text start="9455.12" dur="3.76">countries, they come here to have</text><text start="9456.96" dur="4.16">themselves fixed up. It&amp;#39;s really great.</text><text start="9458.88" dur="4.72">What a great job. Thank you very much.</text><text start="9461.12" dur="5.199">And he&amp;#39;s an auto worker.</text><text start="9463.6" dur="5.12">I met him</text><text start="9466.319" dur="4.801">years ago during the first run. It&amp;#39;s</text><text start="9468.72" dur="3.52">been a long time. The arms look just as</text><text start="9471.12" dur="3.76">good. I don&amp;#39;t know what the hell he</text><text start="9472.24" dur="5.28">does. I guess he lifts up parts. What</text><text start="9474.88" dur="5.599">the hell you do? I want to have those</text><text start="9477.52" dur="4.72">arms. But uh what a great friend he&amp;#39;s</text><text start="9480.479" dur="7.601">been. And right from the beginning, too.</text><text start="9482.24" dur="7.6">He got it. He got it. He got it.</text><text start="9488.08" dur="3.6">And he went right through his union and</text><text start="9489.84" dur="3.92">we won the auto workers and we did</text><text start="9491.68" dur="4.4">great. We didn&amp;#39;t have any support at the</text><text start="9493.76" dur="4.08">top because they were radicalized</text><text start="9496.08" dur="4.319">Democrats, but it didn&amp;#39;t matter. We got</text><text start="9497.84" dur="4.88">the votes at numbers that nobody would</text><text start="9500.399" dur="4.721">believe. The Teamsters also. and right</text><text start="9502.72" dur="4.16">to workers also. We got everything. But</text><text start="9505.12" dur="5.76">you were so great. Thank you very much.</text><text start="9506.88" dur="9.04">That&amp;#39;s beautiful. Special man.</text><text start="9510.88" dur="7.599">So the stock market, just to go on to</text><text start="9515.92" dur="6">something that I love, the stock market</text><text start="9518.479" dur="6.081">hit 88 all-time record highs since the</text><text start="9521.92" dur="5.68">election, much less than two years ago.</text><text start="9524.56" dur="5.759">88 all-time highs. And before you go out</text><text start="9527.6" dur="4.96">and vote for these guys, you have to</text><text start="9530.319" dur="5.12">pick up your 401ks and check them out</text><text start="9532.56" dur="5.919">because they&amp;#39;re 60 and 70% higher than</text><text start="9535.439" dur="5.121">what they were when we just came in</text><text start="9538.479" dur="5.441">through election day. Think take a look</text><text start="9540.56" dur="8.08">at take a look at your 401ks and then go</text><text start="9543.92" dur="7.36">and vote because Obama you lost 25% on</text><text start="9548.64" dur="7.839">your 401ks. With me, you&amp;#39;ve gone up</text><text start="9551.28" dur="8.24">almost 70%. So before you go to vote for</text><text start="9556.479" dur="4.801">John and Mike and all the rest of them,</text><text start="9559.52" dur="4.799">and we have great congressional people</text><text start="9561.28" dur="4.96">here, by the way, income for hardworking</text><text start="9564.319" dur="4.721">Americans has soared to the highest</text><text start="9566.24" dur="4.64">level ever recorded. So I do this thing</text><text start="9569.04" dur="3.92">and it causes a tremendous amount of</text><text start="9570.88" dur="5.04">problems for Secret Service because</text><text start="9572.96" dur="5.76">these next points are so crazy that I</text><text start="9575.92" dur="6.399">don&amp;#39;t have to go anymore. I can save my</text><text start="9578.72" dur="6.48">voice, but I won&amp;#39;t do that. Maybe I will</text><text start="9582.319" dur="6.641">actually. So, think of it. Number one,</text><text start="9585.2" dur="7.199">income for Americans is at the highest</text><text start="9588.96" dur="6.64">point ever. More Americans are working</text><text start="9592.399" dur="5.121">today than at any time in the history of</text><text start="9595.6" dur="3.839">our country. So, more Americans working</text><text start="9597.52" dur="5.12">equity</text><text start="9599.439" dur="4.88">rate has just reached the best ever in</text><text start="9602.64" dur="4.48">the history of our country. That&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="9604.319" dur="6.08">rough one, poverty. But there&amp;#39;s poverty.</text><text start="9607.12" dur="5.12">We have the greatest, strongest we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="9610.399" dur="4.401">ever done. We&amp;#39;ve never done anywhere</text><text start="9612.24" dur="5.68">close on poverty. African-American</text><text start="9614.8" dur="5.04">poverty, Asian-American poverty,</text><text start="9617.92" dur="4.64">Hispanic American poverty, Native</text><text start="9619.84" dur="7.12">American poverty are at the best and</text><text start="9622.56" dur="7.04">lowest levels ever recorded. Exports to</text><text start="9626.96" dur="5.2">our country, think of this, export, we</text><text start="9629.6" dur="4.4">export outside of our we build it.</text><text start="9632.16" dur="4.56">Remember Barack Hussein Obama said,</text><text start="9634" dur="5.6">&amp;quot;We&amp;#39;re not a manufacturing country.&amp;quot;</text><text start="9636.72" dur="5.84">Exports have soared to the highest level</text><text start="9639.6" dur="5.96">in American history.</text><text start="9642.56" dur="3">So,</text><text start="9645.92" dur="4.72">so now what I usually do if I don&amp;#39;t like</text><text start="9648.399" dur="3.92">a crowd, but I always do, we have</text><text start="9650.64" dur="4.08">people. These are the greatest people in</text><text start="9652.319" dur="5.201">the world. We call it the base. The</text><text start="9654.72" dur="4">base. The base is gigantic.</text><text start="9657.52" dur="2.879">And you&amp;#39;re going to see something. We</text><text start="9658.72" dur="4.639">put one little poll up at the end. It&amp;#39;s</text><text start="9660.399" dur="6">so crazy. But the base is gigantic. But</text><text start="9663.359" dur="5.441">so usually what so we just said income&amp;#39;s</text><text start="9666.399" dur="4.721">the highest. We have the highest level</text><text start="9668.8" dur="4.639">of employment. We have the best poverty</text><text start="9671.12" dur="5.359">numbers we&amp;#39;ve ever had. And we have</text><text start="9673.439" dur="4.721">broken the all-time record on exporting</text><text start="9676.479" dur="4.481">meaningfuing</text><text start="9678.16" dur="5.68">things in Michigan and exporting. Right?</text><text start="9680.96" dur="4.56">And usually what I do is I say therefore</text><text start="9683.84" dur="4.8">I don&amp;#39;t have to go on any longer.</text><text start="9685.52" dur="4.64">Goodbye everybody. And I walk out. And</text><text start="9688.64" dur="3.36">I&amp;#39;ve done that a few times and Secret</text><text start="9690.16" dur="4.159">Service goes crazy. You see all these</text><text start="9692" dur="4.8">guys running around. They say, &amp;quot;He&amp;#39;s</text><text start="9694.319" dur="4.641">leaving. He&amp;#39;s leaving. He&amp;#39;s way early.&amp;quot;</text><text start="9696.8" dur="4.72">But now, but it&amp;#39;s those are great</text><text start="9698.96" dur="4.64">numbers. with our Republican Congress. I</text><text start="9701.52" dur="4.08">signed the great big beautiful bill</text><text start="9703.6" dur="4.56">delivering the largest tax cuts in</text><text start="9705.6" dur="5.68">American history, including no tax on</text><text start="9708.16" dur="7.4">tips, no tax on overtime, no tax on</text><text start="9711.28" dur="4.28">social security for our</text><text start="9716" dur="5.359">especially for you because you make so</text><text start="9719.359" dur="4.561">many cars and you you know, not only the</text><text start="9721.359" dur="5.521">new plants, all the plants that you have</text><text start="9723.92" dur="5.92">are expanding. Like I told you about the</text><text start="9726.88" dur="5.68">big 1901 plant with Ford, but they&amp;#39;re</text><text start="9729.84" dur="5.76">all expanding. General Motors, we made</text><text start="9732.56" dur="6.64">interest on car loans taxdeductible, but</text><text start="9735.6" dur="7.64">only if the car is made in America.</text><text start="9739.2" dur="4.04">Okay? Only.</text><text start="9743.52" dur="6.799">Look at these front rows. These front</text><text start="9745.52" dur="8.08">row shows. They&amp;#39;re up to 811 events.</text><text start="9750.319" dur="5.361">You know, I&amp;#39;ve made a lot of them.</text><text start="9753.6" dur="4.08">I&amp;#39;ve done this 26 times. You think it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="9755.68" dur="4.16">easy doing these little suckers? When</text><text start="9757.68" dur="6.96">God made vocal cords, he did not make</text><text start="9759.84" dur="6.8">them for 25 or 26 of these in a period</text><text start="9764.64" dur="4.24">of 10 days.</text><text start="9766.64" dur="6.36">But we have to win. We have to win,</text><text start="9768.88" dur="4.12">right, Mike? We have to win.</text><text start="9774.08" dur="3.64">We got to win.</text><text start="9778.56" dur="5.839">And God did make the vocal cords. I we</text><text start="9782.16" dur="5.44">made the largest ever investment in the</text><text start="9784.399" dur="6.641">US armed forces over $1 trillion. And</text><text start="9787.6" dur="8.16">right here in Michigan, I got 21 new F15</text><text start="9791.04" dur="8.12">EX Eagle twos for Selfridge Air National</text><text start="9795.76" dur="3.4">Guard Base.</text><text start="9803.439" dur="5.04">And that goes with all the other planes</text><text start="9805.439" dur="5.281">we have there. And the Democrats were</text><text start="9808.479" dur="4.721">closing Selfridge down, but I saved</text><text start="9810.72" dur="4.08">thousands of jobs. And really the</text><text start="9813.2" dur="3.68">prestige,</text><text start="9814.8" dur="4.88">the great prestige that comes along with</text><text start="9816.88" dur="5.68">having such a place and only I could</text><text start="9819.68" dur="6.24">have done that. It was requested by a</text><text start="9822.56" dur="6.32">few people both Democrat as you know and</text><text start="9825.92" dur="4.96">and Republican. And I did it. I saved</text><text start="9828.88" dur="5.32">Selfridge. That&amp;#39;s a big deal too. They</text><text start="9830.88" dur="3.32">wanted to</text><text start="9834.96" dur="4.16">Oh, it&amp;#39;s closed. I mean, I saved it. It</text><text start="9836.88" dur="4.72">was was actually effectively closed. The</text><text start="9839.12" dur="4.56">Democrats shut it down and I opened it.</text><text start="9841.6" dur="5.04">We captured and brought to justice the</text><text start="9843.68" dur="7.2">outlaw dictator of Venezuela, Nicholas</text><text start="9846.64" dur="6.719">Maduro, who is now awaiting trial</text><text start="9850.88" dur="4.72">and he&amp;#39;s one of the ones that sent that</text><text start="9853.359" dur="4.401">opened up his prisons and he sent his</text><text start="9855.6" dur="4.64">prisoners in. and we won the war in</text><text start="9857.76" dur="4.48">Venezuela in one day and we are now</text><text start="9860.24" dur="6.079">working with them to produce and we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="9862.24" dur="9.079">getting millions and millions of barrels</text><text start="9866.319" dur="5">of oil every single week from Venezuela.</text><text start="9874.319" dur="4.481">Remember when Russia and China were all</text><text start="9876.479" dur="5.121">over? Everybody was so worried. It&amp;#39;s</text><text start="9878.8" dur="5.04">nearby relatively. They said, &amp;quot;Oh,</text><text start="9881.6" dur="5.2">China&amp;#39;s there. Russia&amp;#39;s there.&amp;quot; No,</text><text start="9883.84" dur="5.2">we&amp;#39;re there. We&amp;#39;re the only one there. I</text><text start="9886.8" dur="6">terminated Barack Hussein and Obama&amp;#39;s</text><text start="9889.04" dur="7.52">JCPOA or Iran nuclear deal, which was a</text><text start="9892.8" dur="6.16">road to Iran having a nuclear weapon. It</text><text start="9896.56" dur="6.24">was the worst agreement and the most</text><text start="9898.96" dur="6.319">dangerous agreement I&amp;#39;ve ever seen. And</text><text start="9902.8" dur="5.2">we obliterated Iran&amp;#39;s nuclear enrichment</text><text start="9905.279" dur="7.801">capacity with Operation Midnight Hammer</text><text start="9908" dur="5.08">and Operation Epic Fury.</text><text start="9915.359" dur="4.801">We defeated them militarily,</text><text start="9917.6" dur="4.719">financially, and otherwise. And now we</text><text start="9920.16" dur="5.119">are ensuring that Iran will never have</text><text start="9922.319" dur="6.16">ever have ever ever ever ever a nuclear</text><text start="9925.279" dur="7.361">weapon. And you&amp;#39;ll see that ending quite</text><text start="9928.479" dur="6.241">soon, one way or the other.</text><text start="9932.64" dur="4">And I got along with Bobby Kennedy and</text><text start="9934.72" dur="4.639">Oz and all the rest of the great people.</text><text start="9936.64" dur="4.639">We did something that was not basically</text><text start="9939.359" dur="4.401">doable. Most other presidents never even</text><text start="9941.279" dur="4.321">tried. they wouldn&amp;#39;t have had a shot. I</text><text start="9943.76" dur="3.599">got most favored nation agreements to</text><text start="9945.6" dur="4.96">reduce the cost of many prescription</text><text start="9947.359" dur="5.12">drugs, all prescription drugs. From the</text><text start="9950.56" dur="5.04">highest drug prices anywhere in the</text><text start="9952.479" dur="5.121">world to the lowest drug prices anywhere</text><text start="9955.6" dur="3.52">in the world, they&amp;#39;re down from 50 to</text><text start="9957.6" dur="3.28">90%.</text><text start="9959.12" dur="4.48">And that makes a tremendous difference.</text><text start="9960.88" dur="4.32">It will you&amp;#39;ll start to see that&amp;#39;s why</text><text start="9963.6" dur="3.28">we have to win because I don&amp;#39;t want them</text><text start="9965.2" dur="4.56">to get credit for it. You know, so many</text><text start="9966.88" dur="4.64">things I did and we did and they, you</text><text start="9969.76" dur="4.4">know, they statutoily they kick in</text><text start="9971.52" dur="4.32">later. I said, &amp;quot;Boy, oh boy, I&amp;#39;d hate</text><text start="9974.16" dur="3.199">I&amp;#39;d hate to have this stuff kick in with</text><text start="9975.84" dur="3.12">somebody else where they take credit.&amp;quot;</text><text start="9977.359" dur="3.12">But they tried to do that. But</text><text start="9978.96" dur="3.6">ultimately, the people know and that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="9980.479" dur="4.081">why we&amp;#39;re here. That&amp;#39;s why we won the</text><text start="9982.56" dur="4.719">White House and that&amp;#39;s why we won it.</text><text start="9984.56" dur="7.68">Every single swing state, the popular</text><text start="9987.279" dur="7.921">vote, the 87% of the counties, a massive</text><text start="9992.24" dur="4.64">electoral college win.</text><text start="9995.2" dur="3.84">Think of it. All seven swing states. You</text><text start="9996.88" dur="4">remember they said, &amp;quot;Well, Trump needs</text><text start="9999.04" dur="3.6">two of the swing states to win.&amp;quot; I got</text><text start="10000.88" dur="6.88">all seven.</text><text start="10002.64" dur="7.2">We got We got all seven. We got</text><text start="10007.76" dur="3.92">We abolished all discriminatory</text><text start="10009.84" dur="5.2">diversity, equity, and inclusion</text><text start="10011.68" dur="6.96">policies. All of this, if they win, will</text><text start="10015.04" dur="6.399">be all this junk. Open borders, men and</text><text start="10018.64" dur="4.719">women sports, transgender for everybody.</text><text start="10021.439" dur="4.081">It&amp;#39;s all going to be put right back in.</text><text start="10023.359" dur="3.92">as soon as they win. They win, you got</text><text start="10025.52" dur="4.32">it right back. So, it&amp;#39;s you you will</text><text start="10027.279" dur="4.08">only have yourselves to blame. And I</text><text start="10029.84" dur="3.84">don&amp;#39;t think there&amp;#39;s any coming back from</text><text start="10031.359" dur="3.681">that either. I think if they if they did</text><text start="10033.68" dur="4.16">that, I don&amp;#39;t think there&amp;#39;d be any</text><text start="10035.04" dur="5.6">coming back. We did a great job to win.</text><text start="10037.84" dur="6.16">We did an amazing job together to win.</text><text start="10040.64" dur="5.679">It wasn&amp;#39;t easy. We had a fake press.</text><text start="10044" dur="3.92">We had a fake press, a disgraceful</text><text start="10046.319" dur="3.521">press.</text><text start="10047.92" dur="4.399">We had those open borders where people</text><text start="10049.84" dur="6.08">were pouring in by 25 million people</text><text start="10052.319" dur="6.321">came in and uh many of them were very</text><text start="10055.92" dur="4.88">bad very bad bad criminals. We got</text><text start="10058.64" dur="4.799">critical race theory and transgender</text><text start="10060.8" dur="5.96">insanity the hell out of our schools. We</text><text start="10063.439" dur="3.321">did it quickly</text><text start="10069.359" dur="3.601">and we made English the official</text><text start="10071.2" dur="5.48">language of the United States of</text><text start="10072.96" dur="3.72">America. Thank you.</text><text start="10078.399" dur="4.96">And our country is doing so well under</text><text start="10081.279" dur="4.561">Republican leadership that only I can</text><text start="10083.359" dur="4.881">make you this promise. The Democrats</text><text start="10085.84" dur="4.08">can&amp;#39;t do it because this country will go</text><text start="10088.24" dur="3.52">to hell.</text><text start="10089.92" dur="4.399">If Republicans win the House of</text><text start="10091.76" dur="5.12">Representatives and the United States</text><text start="10094.319" dur="6.721">Senate, I am going to give all adult</text><text start="10096.88" dur="7.8">citizens in the United States $5,000.</text><text start="10101.04" dur="3.64">You deserve it.</text><text start="10108.8" dur="5.36">And only Republicans can do it.</text><text start="10111.359" dur="4.96">Democrats can&amp;#39;t because we&amp;#39;re taking in</text><text start="10114.16" dur="4.96">massive amounts of money through tariffs</text><text start="10116.319" dur="6">and record setting economic success like</text><text start="10119.12" dur="5.76">you&amp;#39;ve just heard. And that&amp;#39;s peanuts. I</text><text start="10122.319" dur="4.321">could name I could name factories all</text><text start="10124.88" dur="4.559">day long and plants that are being</text><text start="10126.64" dur="5.52">built. Pharmaceutical plants, Eli, Lily,</text><text start="10129.439" dur="5.681">Merc, Fizer. pharmaceutical plants are</text><text start="10132.