 to do</text><text start="11348.08" dur="3.44">with candidates. It has nothing to do.</text><text start="11350.08" dur="3.279">It&amp;#39;s just love. The love that we have</text><text start="11351.52" dur="2.959">for each other. So, let me see those</text><text start="11353.359" dur="4.401">charts, please.</text><text start="11354.479" dur="6.081">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Okay. MAGA GOP on Trump. In the 2024</text><text start="11357.76" dur="4.96">election versus Kla Harris, he got 99%</text><text start="11360.56" dur="3.52">of the MAGA GOP vote. Perhaps</text><text start="11362.72" dur="4.16">surprisingly, I might have thought it&amp;#39;d</text><text start="11364.08" dur="4.239">be 100%, but it was 99%.</text><text start="11366.88" dur="4.64">Compare that to his approval rating.</text><text start="11368.319" dur="5.841">Now, at the MAGA GOP, it&amp;#39;s 98%. That is,</text><text start="11371.52" dur="4.4">there&amp;#39;s been no real decline in MAGA</text><text start="11374.16" dur="3.04">support. These folks say that they&amp;#39;re</text><text start="11375.92" dur="3.519">going to vote for congressional</text><text start="11377.2" dur="4.72">Republicans come the midterm elections.</text><text start="11379.439" dur="4.641">Again, that&amp;#39;s the 99% that Trump got</text><text start="11381.92" dur="4.479">against Kla Harris. Look, now in terms</text><text start="11384.08" dur="3.76">of the congressional vote, 98% of them</text><text start="11386.399" dur="3.441">say they&amp;#39;re going to be voting for House</text><text start="11387.84" dur="4.32">Republican candidates. So, that support</text><text start="11389.84" dur="4.559">is actually really holding up strong.</text><text start="11392.16" dur="4.8">It&amp;#39;s really, really strong when it comes</text><text start="11394.399" dur="4.641">to MAGA GOP and Republicans holding on</text><text start="11396.96" dur="4.8">to that vote. This one, okay, the</text><text start="11399.04" dur="4.319">president Republicans m